ML Monitoring Dashboard for Fraud Detection
Overview
This project sets up and deploys a Grafana monitoring dashboard for the xFusionCorp Industries ML platform team. The dashboard tracks the rolling prediction accuracy (prediction_accuracy) of the fraud-detection model using a pre-provisioned Prometheus data source.

Project Structure
dashboard.json: The complete JSON definition for the Grafana dashboard containing the timeseries panel targeting the Prometheus metric.

Deployment & Verification Scripts: API curl commands used to programmatically register and verify the dashboard state.

1. Dashboard Configuration (dashboard.json)
JSON
{
  "dashboard": {
    "id": null,
    "uid": "fraud-detection-ml",
    "title": "ML Monitoring Dashboard",
    "tags": ["ml", "fraud"],
    "timezone": "browser",
    "panels": [
      {
        "id": 1,
        "type": "timeseries",
        "title": "Prediction Accuracy Over Time",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "targets": [
          {
            "datasource": {
              "type": "prometheus",
              "uid": "prometheus"
            },
            "expr": "prediction_accuracy",
            "refId": "A"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "schemaVersion": 38,
    "version": 1
  },
  "overwrite": true
}
2. Terminal Automation Scripts
Step A: Create the Dashboard Configuration File
Run the following bash script to write the dashboard structure locally:

Bash
cat << 'EOF' > dashboard.json
{
  "dashboard": {
    "id": null,
    "uid": "fraud-detection-ml",
    "title": "ML Monitoring Dashboard",
    "tags": ["ml", "fraud"],
    "timezone": "browser",
    "panels": [
      {
        "id": 1,
        "type": "timeseries",
        "title": "Prediction Accuracy Over Time",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "targets": [
          {
            "datasource": {
              "type": "prometheus",
              "uid": "prometheus"
            },
            "expr": "prediction_accuracy",
            "refId": "A"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "schemaVersion": 38,
    "version": 1
  },
  "overwrite": true
}
EOF
Step B: Push the Dashboard to Grafana via HTTP API
Deploy the dashboard directly into the local Grafana instance running on port 3000 using admin credentials (admin / grafana2026):

Bash
curl -X POST \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -u "admin:grafana2026" \
  -d @dashboard.json \
  http://localhost:3000/api/dashboards/db
Step C: Verify Dashboard Registration
Query the Grafana search API to ensure the dashboard is successfully created and indexed:

Bash
curl -u "admin:grafana2026" http://localhost:3000/api/search?type=dash-db
